## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests end-to-end 3D understanding of dense retail shelves and edge adaptation for unseen products.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose with template-based fit
- Synthetic+real data strategy for crowded shelves
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with lightweight adapters
- Occlusion-aware pose and neighbor interaction modeling

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(input) {
  const features = backbone(input);
  const detections = detectorHead(features);
  const poses = poseHead(features, detections);
  return {detections, poses};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How do you handle multiple identical items and permutation ambiguity?
- How would you evaluate robustness to lighting and glare on glossy shelves?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical on-device CV with privacy constraints, latency pressure, and data privacy.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight models, ROI extraction, temporal reasoning
- Quantization, pruning, on-device inference
- Federated learning, differential privacy, privacy budgets
- Evaluation: latency, memory, F1/precision-recall under occlusion

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: frame window prep for on-device gesture model
function prepareWindow(frames) {
  const ROI = detectHandROI(frames[0]);
  const window = frames.slice(-16).map(f => crop(f, ROI));
  return stack(window);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and mitigate drift when lighting changes across devices?
- How would you handle new gestures without retraining all devices?

